    "faq_compare": {
      "type": "cp-product-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "comp_1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which Carepod is right for me?",
            "answer": "<p>Here's a quick guide:<br><br><strong>Cube Plus</strong> — Our flagship model. Best for those who want the most advanced features including warm mist, built-in sanitization, auto-humidity control, and night mode. Covers up to 700 sq ft.<br><br><strong>One Plus</strong> — Our most popular model. A sleek, modern design with a powerful mist output. Great for bedrooms and living rooms up to 500 sq ft.<br><br><strong>One</strong> — The original Carepod. Same stainless steel quality and coverage as One Plus in the classic cylindrical design. Up to 500 sq ft.<br><br><strong>Mini</strong> — Compact and portable. Perfect for nurseries, desks, dorm rooms, or travel. Covers up to 350 sq ft.</p>",
            "open_default": false
          }
        },
        "comp_2": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between Carepod One and One Plus?",
            "answer": "<p>Both the One and One Plus use the same stainless steel tank, oscillator technology, and 3-part cleaning design. They cover the same room size (up to 500 sq ft) and offer the same tank capacity (2.3L). The One Plus features an updated, more modern exterior design with refined aesthetics and a slightly smaller footprint. Functionally, they deliver the same clean mist performance. Choose the One Plus if you prefer the newer design, or the One if you love the original classic look.</p>",
            "open_default": false
          }
        },
        "comp_3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between Cube Plus and One Plus?",
            "answer": "<p>The Cube Plus is our premium model with several additional features:<br><br><strong>Warm Mist:</strong> The Cube Plus can produce warm mist in addition to cool mist. The One Plus is cool mist only.<br><strong>Built-in Sanitization:</strong> The Cube Plus heats water to 158°F to kill 99.9% of bacteria automatically. The One Plus relies on manual cleaning (boiling).<br><strong>Auto Humidity Control:</strong> The Cube Plus has a built-in hygrometer that automatically adjusts mist output to maintain your desired humidity level.<br><strong>Night Mode:</strong> Dims the display and operates at the quietest setting.<br><strong>Coverage:</strong> Cube Plus covers 700 sq ft vs. 500 sq ft for the One Plus.<br><br>Choose the One Plus for a streamlined cool-mist experience, or the Cube Plus for the most complete feature set.</p>",
            "open_default": false
          }
        },
        "comp_4": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does the Cube Plus have warm mist?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. The Cube Plus is the only Carepod model that offers both warm and cool mist. The warm mist mode heats water before dispersing it, which can feel more comfortable during cold winter months and may help soothe congestion. You can switch between warm and cool mist modes at any time using the control panel. Note: when using warm mist mode around children or pets, place the unit on an elevated surface out of reach.</p>",
            "open_default": false
          }
        },
        "comp_5": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the mood light feature?",
            "answer": "<p>Select Carepod models include an ambient mood light built into the base or body of the unit. This soft LED light can cycle through colors or be set to a single color, creating a calming atmosphere — especially nice in nurseries or bedrooms at night. The light can be turned off entirely if you prefer complete darkness. It's a subtle design touch that adds to the overall experience without affecting humidification performance.</p>",
            "open_default": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": ["comp_1", "comp_2", "comp_3", "comp_4", "comp_5"],
