    "faq_technical": {
      "type": "cp-product-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "tech_1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the wattage / power consumption?",
            "answer": "<p>Carepod is energy-efficient and designed for continuous use:<br><br><strong>Cube Plus:</strong> 25W (cool mist) / 110W (warm mist) / 280W (sanitization cycle)<br><strong>One Plus:</strong> 25W<br><strong>One:</strong> 25W<br><strong>Mini:</strong> 18W<br><br>At 25W on cool mist mode, running Carepod 24 hours a day would cost roughly $0.07 per day (based on average US electricity rates). All models use a standard AC power adapter and plug into a regular household outlet.</p>",
            "open_default": false
          }
        },
        "tech_2": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does Carepod have auto shut-off?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, all Carepod models include an automatic shut-off safety feature. When the water level drops below the minimum threshold, the unit will turn itself off to prevent the motor from running dry. This protects the oscillator disc from damage and means you can safely leave your Carepod running overnight or while you're away without worry. Simply refill the tank and turn it back on when you're ready.</p>",
            "open_default": false
          }
        },
        "tech_3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use a timer with Carepod?",
            "answer": "<p>The Cube Plus features a built-in timer function that allows you to set the unit to run for a specific duration (2, 4, 6, or 8 hours) before automatically turning off. The One, One Plus, and Mini do not have built-in timers, but you can use an external smart plug or outlet timer to achieve the same effect. Pair it with a smart plug like a TP-Link or Wemo to control your Carepod with voice assistants or automated schedules.</p>",
            "open_default": false
          }
        },
        "tech_4": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the oscillator and how does it work?",
            "answer": "<p>The oscillator (also called the ultrasonic disc or vibration plate) is the component that creates the mist. It sits at the bottom of the water tank and vibrates at an ultrasonic frequency — over 1.7 million times per second. This rapid vibration breaks water into micro-fine droplets (1-5 microns in diameter) that are light enough to float in the air as a cool, visible mist. The oscillator disc in Carepod is made of ceramic and stainless steel, is easily removable for cleaning, and is designed to last for years of continuous use. If it ever needs replacing, you can order a replacement disc from our store.</p>",
            "open_default": false
          }
        }
      },
